<title>FRANCE: Ecia shares down after ratings cut.</title>
<headline>Ecia shares down after ratings cut.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in car parts manufacturer Ecia, controlled by the PSA Peugeot Citroen group, fell on Tuesday after analysts cut their ratings, portfolio managers said.</p>
<p>They said CPR Finance described Ecia's 10 percent half-year sales rise to 5.5 billion francs as excellent but cut its rating to sell (2) from (1), citing the stock's 45 percent rise so far this year.</p>
<p>Massonaud also cut its rating to sell from buy, citing the stock's advance and recommended switching into other suppliers such as Valeo, Sommer Allibert and Bertrand Faure.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
